sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor U as User
    participant UI as superchat.el
    participant D as Dispatcher
    participant R as Runtime
    participant T as Tape/SQLite
    participant L as llm adapter
    participant P as Provider(curl)
    participant A as Authority
    participant C as Closure

    U->>UI: C-c C-c
    UI->>D: send-input
    D->>D: parse prefixes / attach memories / compose-request
    D->>R: runtime-submit(request)
    R->>R: validate-request, mint session/turn/run ids, registry := accepted
    R->>T: intent.received
    R->>T: run.started (causation=intent)
    R-->>D: {run-id, turn-id, status:accepted} (returns immediately)
    R->>L: llm-generate-answer (observer/tool context dynamically bound)
    L->>P: streaming request
    P-->>UI: chunk → stream-function render (liveness checked per chunk)

    Note over L,A: llm.el runs the tool loop natively, every tool crosses the gate
    P-->>L: tool_call
    L->>A: invoke tool via wrapper
    A->>T: tool.requested (persisted before any decision)
    A->>A: classify effects → compose policies (tighten-only)
    alt allow
        A->>A: execute
    else ask
        A->>T: approval.requested (with SHA-256 request hash)
        A->>U: y-or-n-p
        A->>T: approval.decided
    end
    A->>T: tool.execution.started → tool.completed/failed
    A-->>L: result back into llm prompt, loop continues

    P-->>L: terminal text
    L->>R: observer('terminal)
    R->>T: response.completed
    R->>R: turn hooks (before the terminal event)
    R->>C: guard: replay full Session, judge ready-terminal
    C-->>R: proved → allow, otherwise signal → Run becomes audit-incomplete
    R->>T: run.completed / failed / cancelled
    R->>T: turn.completed
    Note over R,UI: delivery strictly after the durable terminal facts
    R->>UI: deliver (failure demoted to warning, durable facts unaffected)
    R->>R: completion hooks → release (kill ephemeral buffer)
    R->>C: shadow: durable-run-terminal cross-check (double-isolated, record only)
